<title>USA: Ascent Q4 oper, net and shr loss widen.</title>
<headline>Ascent Q4 oper, net and shr loss widen.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in millions, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>			    Three Months Ended  Twelve Months Ended</p>
<p>						Dec. 31	 Dec. 31</p>
<p>					1996     1995     1996     1995</p>
<p> Revenues			  $91.6    $59.7   $258.1   $201.8</p>
<p> Operating Expenses	     91.8     56.3    227.6    164.6</p>
<p>Depreciation and amortization</p>
<p>					25.6     14.9     74.8     53.7</p>
<p> Provision for Restructuring   0.0	0.0	0.0     10.9</p>
<p> Operating Loss		 (25.8)   (11.5)   (44.3)   (27.4)</p>
<p> Interest expense		(4.8)    (0.4)   (10.7)    (0.8)</p>
<p> Other income (expense), net   0.1    (0.2)	0.5    (2.0)</p>
<p>loss before taxes, minority interest</p>
<p>  &amp; extraordinary loss	(30.5)   (12.1)   (54.5)   (30.2)</p>
<p> Income tax benefit		4.7	4.3     12.0	9.8</p>
<p>Loss before minority interest</p>
<p>  and extraordinary loss    (25.8)    (7.8)   (42.5)   (20.4)</p>
<p> Minority interest		 7.1    (0.1)	6.8    (0.6)</p>
<p>Extraordinary loss on early</p>
<p>extinguishment of debt,</p>
<p>  net of taxes		   (0.3)	0.0    (0.3)	0.0</p>
<p> Net loss			( 19.0)   ( 7.9)  ( 36.0)  ( 21.0)</p>
<p> EBITDA			   ( 0.2)	3.4     30.5     37.2</p>
<p> Net loss per share	  ( 0.64)  ( 0.32)  ( 1.21)  ( 0.87)</p>
<p> EBITDA per share	    ( 0.01)     0.14     1.03     1.54</p>
<p>Weighted average number of</p>
<p>  common shares outstanding   29.8     24.9     29.8     24.2</p>
<p>NOTES: The company restated its 1995 financial statements, and as a result 1995 net loss increased from $19.5 million, or a loss of $0.80 per share, to $21 million, or a loss of $0.87 per share.</p>
<p>The restatement lowered 1995 EBITDA from $40.8 million to $37.2 million and Q4 1995 EBITDA from $7.0 million to $3.4 million. EBITDA is earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation and amortization.</p>
<p>EBITDA for Q4 1996 decreased $3.6 million, or 105 percent, from $3.4 million in 1995 Q4, as restated. Excluding about $6.7 million in charges at On Command, EBITDA for the year would have stayed constant at $37.2 million, and EBITDA for Q4 1996 would have increased 91 percent to $6.5 million.</p>
<p>Full company name is Ascent Entertainment Group Inc.</p>
